---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PrevalenceChart from "../components/PrevalenceChart.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Results — What Limits Us?">
  <h1>Results &amp; Findings</h1>
  <p class="intro">
    Empirical findings from analyzing 16,047 ACL and EMNLP papers (2020–2025)
    and their self-reported limitations using our iterative hybrid coding pipeline.
  </p>

  <section class="results-section">
    <h2>Most common limitations</h2>
    <p class="section-desc">
      Distribution of limitation codes across all 16,047 papers. Authors frequently report
      methodological constraints and scope limitations, but also use the section for rhetorical
      purposes (e.g. framing future work or contextualizing achievements).
    </p>
    <PrevalenceChart />
  </section>

  <section class="results-section upcoming-section">
    <h2>Temporal trends (RQ1)</h2>
    <div class="card">
      <span class="badge-upcoming">In preparation</span>
      <h3>The 2022 Policy Divergence</h3>
      <p>
        Before late 2022, <em>Methodological Constraints</em> was the predominant code.
        Following mandatory policy adoption at EMNLP 2022 and ACL 2023, <em>Scope Limitation</em>
        surged past 65%, with the two codes swapping ranks almost exactly at the policy boundary.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="results-section upcoming-section">
    <h2>Track &amp; Affiliation Patterns (RQ2)</h2>
    <div class="card">
      <span class="badge-upcoming">In preparation</span>
      <h3>Field-Wide Homogeneity &amp; Affiliation Differences</h3>
      <p>
        Despite diverse research areas, a chi-square test of homogeneity reveals that limitation reporting
        is remarkably uniform across 29 tracks (&chi;&sup2;(1,092) = 2,872, p &lt; 0.001, Cram&eacute;r's V = 0.071).
        Meanwhile, corporate vs. non-corporate affiliations show notable differences in resource constraint disclosures.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="results-section upcoming-section">
    <h2>Inter-annotator Agreement</h2>
    <div class="card">
      <span class="badge-upcoming">In preparation</span>
      <h3>Per-Code Reliability Breakdown</h3>
      <p>
        Full per-code Krippendorff's &alpha; breakdown across all 50 codes on the 150-paper
        human-annotated reference benchmark, comparing inter-human baseline with model-augmented consensus.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .intro {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .results-section {
    margin: 2.5rem 0;
    padding-bottom: 2rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .results-section:last-of-type {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .section-desc {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .upcoming-section .card {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-border) 15%, transparent);
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }

  .badge-upcoming {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-border) 40%, transparent);
    padding: 0.15rem 0.5rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .card h3 {
    margin: 0.25rem 0 0.5rem;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }

  .card p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
</style>
